{
  "prepared": "2026-09-17",
  "scope": "DAPHNE control, configuration and published monitoring over one shared 1 Gb Ethernet link; HD and VD. Data readout and optical timing transport excluded.",
  "author_design_decisions": [
    "One board CCM Ethernet connection through switch to physical server; retain daphne-icd SFP baseline",
    "FD-VD: 1344 channels / 32 channels per board = 42 boards; FD-HD: 6000 / 40 = 150 boards",
    "DAQ CCM controls run variables and timing-endpoint settings through the configuration component integrated into the external OPC UA server; Hermes receives configuration on its separate IPBus/UDP endpoint; it does not publish counters",
    "Configuration and control use request/response; all monitoring is published",
    "daphne-server publishes firmware counters, timing state and applied readout configuration through the OPC UA server to DAQ opmon; SC monitors voltages, temperatures, fans, service status and versions",
    "Local timing-endpoint configuration and monitoring traverse the same GbE link; DAQ configuration path exposes recovery to SC",
    "SC publishes board readiness from current board-generated timing and recovery evidence",
    "Only the protocol architecture diagram is retained; no detailed variable inventory or optical timing/readout description",
    "Use DUNE-DAQ/daphne-os for daphne-server, Protobuf schemas, endpoint recovery documentation and runtime services."
  ],
